00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Under the Skin is a thriller, science fiction, drama
film directed by Jonathan Glazer.

2
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
A seductive stranger prowls the streets of Glasgow in search of
prey: unsuspecting men who fall under her spell.

3
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Under the Skin is a 2013  science fiction film directed by Jonathan Glazer and written
by Glazer and Walter Campbell, based on the 2000 novel by Michel Faber.

4
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
It stars Scarlett Johansson as a female extraterrestrial disguised as a
human who preys on lone men in the evening hours in Scotland.

5
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
The film premiered at the Telluride Film Festival on 29 August 2013.

6
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
It was released in the United Kingdom on 14 March 2014,
and in other territories later in the year.

7
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
Glazer developed Under the Skin for over a decade.

8
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
He and Campbell pared it back from an elaborate, effects-heavy concept to a
sparse story focusing on an alien perspective of the human condition.

9
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Most of the cast had no acting experience, and many
scenes were filmed with hidden cameras.

10
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The film was a box-office failure, grossing $7.2
million on a budget of $13.3 million.

11
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
Under the Skin was widely acclaimed by critics for Glazer’s direction,
Johansson's performance, Landin’s cinematography, and Mica Levi's score.

12
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
It received numerous accolades and awards, was named the best film of the year by various critics and publications, appeared on
many best-of-the-decade lists, and was ranked 61st on the BBC's 100 Greatest Films of the 21st Century list.

13
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:51,000
It has subsequently been regarded as one of the best
films of the 2010s and the 21st century.

